Terms: the same trip records are a public data set on NYC Open Data
("2024 Yellow Taxi Trip Data", https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/rwwi-khbc).
NYC Administrative Code § 23-502(d) (Open Data Law, Local Law 11 of 2012)
requires such public data sets to be "made available without any registration
requirement, license requirement or restrictions on their use". No formal open
licence is attached; the AWS Open Data Registry
(https://registry.opendata.aws/nyc-tlc-trip-records-pds/) points to the NYC.gov
Terms of Use (https://www.nyc.gov/main/terms-of-use), whose all-rights-reserved
clause covers site materials rather than open data sets. Source credited as
asked by the registry: New York City Taxi and Limousine Commission (TLC) Trip
Record Data. The records contain no personal data: only times, TLC zone IDs
and fares.

Disclaimer from TLC: "The trip data was not created by the TLC, and TLC makes
no representations as to the accuracy of these data."

sample.jsonl.zst holds every 148th row (20 032 trips) of the file above,
with columns renamed to snake_case and parquet timestamps read as UTC.
Regenerate it with:

    go run ./cmd/fetch -dataset nyctaxi
    go test ./datasets/nyctaxi -update "$PWD/data/nyctaxi/yellow_tripdata_2024-01.parquet"
